    "description": "Candidate for the first COVID Hub submission, 7 November 2026. Equal mixture of four recipes, each refit on all of 2022-23 through 2025-26 with finalized future admissions and ED labels, ten seeds (42-51) each: (1) width-192 sampled MLP with neighbouring-state exchange and artificial reporting errors on half of training episodes; (2) width-256 direct-quantile model with a GRU encoder, a US-only summary shared with states, and reporting errors on 25% of episodes; (3) width-256 direct-quantile MLP with finalized training histories, a US-only summary and multiscale signal features; (4) width-256 direct-quantile MLP with neighbouring-state exchange, errors on half of episodes and weight decay 1e-4. No covariates. Deployment uses corrected reported inputs. Not yet submitted.",
